{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A force-directed drawing by Fruchterman and Reingold’s spring embedder, from positions","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"drawn uniformly in [0, 1)² from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"generator"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/fruchtermanReingoldLayout(iterations:optimalDistance:threshold:barnesHutTheta:weight:using:)"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"fruchtermanReingoldLayout"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"iterations"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 50, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"optimalDistance"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"threshold"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 1e-4, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"barnesHutTheta"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double"},{"kind":"text","text":" = { _ in 1 }, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"using"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"generator"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"inout"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SG","text":"RandomNumberGenerator"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Drawing","text":"Drawing"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every pair of vertices repels with force k²\/d and every edge attracts its ends with force"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"type":"text","text":" · d²\/k, where d is their distance (at least 0.01) and k is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"optimalDistance"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(default √(1\/n)). Each step moves every vertex along its net force by at most the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"temperature, which starts at a tenth of the larger side of the start’s bounding box (k\/10"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when every vertex starts at one point) and falls by the same amount each step, reaching 0"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"after "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"iterations + 1"},{"type":"text","text":" steps. Two vertices at exactly the same point repel as if 0.01"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"apart, along a direction fixed by their two "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" offsets, so coincident vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"separate deterministically. The run stops after "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"iterations"},{"type":"text","text":" steps, or earlier once the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"moves’ root-sum-square divided by n is below "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"threshold"},{"type":"text","text":". Self-loops are ignored; parallel edges"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"add their weights. The drawing is in layout units (vertices end about k apart), not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rescaled. A directed graph is drawn through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"undirectedView"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The start takes exactly 2n draws: x then y for each vertex in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" order, each the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"top 53 bits of one ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"next()"},{"text":". The same generator state gives the same drawing. Positions are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not stable across library versions, because the iteration is chaotic and any change in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"summation order changes its digits.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Repulsion is exact by default: O(n²) per step, for graphs up to a few thousand vertices."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"barnesHutTheta: θ"},{"type":"text","text":" approximates it with a Barnes–Hut quadtree, O(n log n) per step: a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"square cell of side s whose centre of mass is at distance D from the vertex, and which does"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not contain the vertex, acts as one body when s\/D < θ. θ = 1.2 suits graphs past about 5,000 vertices;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"θ = 0 is exact repulsion."}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Fruchterman and Reingold, “Graph drawing by force-directed placement”, Software: Practice","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and Experience 21(11), 1991.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Barnes and Hut, “A hierarchical O(N log N) force-calculation algorithm”, Nature 324,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"1986.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"O(iterations · (n² + m)) time exactly, O(iterations · (n log n + m)) with Barnes–Hut; O(n + m)","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"memory.","type":"text"}]},{"style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"iterations ≥ 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"code":"optimalDistance","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", when given, is positive and finite;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"threshold ≥ 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"code":"barnesHutTheta","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", when given, is finite and not negative; every weight","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is finite and not negative.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","name":"Precondition"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/graphprotocols\/graph\/fruchtermanreingoldlayout(iterations:optimaldistance:threshold:barneshuttheta:weight:using:)"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawi